      "claim": "FIXED",
      "final_text": "Sprint now stops on the same tick you release W. Before, it waited one tick. The visible regression suite (25 scenarios) and the unit tests pass, and a flat-floor sprint-then-release scenario matches the oracle exactly.\n\nThere were two edits in `sim/src/mcsim/player.py`:\n- **The bug:** the stop check used last tick's forward state (`was_forward`), so sprint lasted one tick too long. It now uses the current tick's forward state.\n- **Reordering:** with only that change, three wall scenarios diverged (sprint stayed on while holding forward into the wall). I moved the \"start sprinting\" check ahead of the \"stop sprinting\" check, so a collision stop sticks for that tick. This is also what the oracle expects.\n\nThe `was_forward` variable is now unused in `tick()`; I left it in place.\n\nSTATUS: FIXED",
